# Wave 5 follow-on. A correction to the landed sectionsByKind table.
#
# The core pillar's inspectorModel drifted from its spec on two kinds and
# nothing caught it: verify checks structural wiring, and a list of section
# names inside a function body is not wiring. The core pillar's own tests
# asserted the node and edge lists and not the other two, which is the hole
# that let it through.
#
# It matters now rather than then, because this pillar ships the Shape and
# Line sections. Without the correction, an annotation selection never names
# 'shape' or 'line', renderableSections therefore never surfaces them, and
# ShapeSection, LineSection and the annotation branches of commitShape and
# commitLine are unreachable from the UI while looking fully wired.

file: "packages/editor/src/inspector/model.ts"
doc: "Selection -> which inspector sections apply, and to which ids."

methods: [
  { name: "inspectorModel"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Only the sectionsByKind table changes. The empty-selection and\n"
      "mixed-kind guards, the kind check and the id mapping are unchanged.\n"
      "\n"
      "The table must be exactly this, in exactly this order -- the order IS\n"
      "the display order, and the panel takes it from here:\n"
      "\n"
      "  node        layout, shape, typography\n"
      "  group       layout, group, shape, typography\n"
      "  edge        line, typography\n"
      "  annotation  layout, annotation, shape, line, typography\n"
      "\n"
      "Two corrections against what is currently in the file:\n"
      "\n"
      "ANNOTATION GAINS 'shape' AND 'line'. An annotation has a Glyph2D\n"
      "(`shape`) and a Glyph1D (`callout`) in the schema, and\n"
      "patchAnnotationEntry already carries both. Omitting them was an error,\n"
      "not a scope decision.\n"
      "\n"
      "GROUP'S 'group' ENTRY MOVES to second, directly after layout. Its\n"
      "fields -- padding, render mode, label position -- are container\n"
      "geometry, so they belong beside layout rather than after the paint\n"
      "sections.\n"
      "\n"
      "Neither the 'group' nor the 'annotation' section has a component yet;\n"
      "renderableSections filters them out. Naming them here is still correct\n"
      "-- this table describes what the DOMAIN has, and the registry\n"
      "separately describes what the panel can draw. Conflating the two is\n"
      "what would make the missing sections invisible rather than merely\n"
      "unbuilt."
    inputs: [
      { name: "selection", type: { named: { symbol: "Array", args: [{ named: { symbol: "ElementRef" } }] } } }
    ]
    output: { unsupported: { reason: UNION_AT_TYPE_POSITION, source_excerpt: "InspectorModel | undefined" } }
  }
]
